<article class="env-proposition" id="F532CC">
       
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F532CC">Proposition <span data-tag="F532CC">2.2.1.1</span>.</a><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
Let $p: S' \rightarrow S$ be a map of simplicial sets, $\calC $ a simplicial category, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a simplicial functor, and let $\phi ': \sCoNerve [S'] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ denote the composition $\phi \circ \sCoNerve [p]$. Let $p_{!}: (\sSet )_{/S'} \rightarrow (\sSet )_{/S}$ denote the forgetful functor, given by composition with $p$. There is a natural isomorphism of functors 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  St_{\phi } \circ p_{!} \simeq St_{\phi '} \]
</div>
<p>
 from $(\sSet )_{/S'}$ to $\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\pi : \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ a simplicial functor between simplicial categories, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a simplicial functor. Then there is a natural isomorphism of functors 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ St_{\pi ^{op} \circ \phi } \simeq \pi _{!} \circ St_{\phi } \]
</div>
<p>
 from $(\sSet )_{/S}$ to $\Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '}$. Here $\pi _{!}: \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC } \rightarrow \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '}$ is the left adjoint to the functor $\pi ^{\ast }: \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC '} \rightarrow \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }$ given by composition with $\pi $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
